    <briefdescription>
<para>Define sets of equivalent particles. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Particles in an equivalency set are assumed to be equivalent under exchange. Given that, one should only generate each of the equivalent conformations once. More specifically, given equivalent particles p0 and p1, if p0 is given state s0 and p1 is given state s1, then p1 will never be given state s0 when p0 is given the state s1. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
